1. DEFINITIONS

"Software" means EDNA-1 (Enhanced Detection & Neural Analysis), including but not limited to
the source code (src/edna.js), the MCP server (mcp/), SDK and TypeScript definitions
(src/edna.d.ts), the profile-hash module (src/profile-hash.js), PWA templates (pwa/), the
verification harness and test vectors (verification/), documentation, the 16 behavioral
signal weights, the consensus logic, and the "Human Proof Seal" design.

"Licensor" means SEBKLAEY© Agency, represented by Sebastian Kläy (@sebklaey),
sebklay@me.com.

"Evaluation" means downloading, running and testing the Software on your own devices,
solely to assess its functionality — non-commercially and without production deployment.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software or any part of it (i) in a production
environment, (ii) in any product or service offered for consideration, (iii) within any
revenue-generating business process, (iv) by any legal entity other than pure evaluation,
or (v) as a component of AI-provider, platform or enterprise infrastructure.

